  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted → 67.8% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes meaningful signal over RNA alone. config_002 is a clean single-variable ablation of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool) but removes the image branch entirely. If rna_only matches or exceeds 67.8%, the remaining 8 experiments should pivot toward RNA-encoder and aggregation variants; if multimodal clearly wins, the budget should focus on optimizing image encoder, fusion, and aggregation within the multimodal family. Resolving this fundamental architectural question early maximizes the information value of the next 8 experiments and prevents wasting budget on multimodal refinements that may not be warranted."
}

